      "name": "ClearBitArrayRange",
      "signature": "int ClearBitArrayRange(dword * pBitmapBase, int nBitOffset)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Process bitmap bits from specified offset through end of buffer\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate word index (nBitOffset / 32) and bit offset within word (nBitOffset % 32)\n2. Create bit mask for starting position: 1 << (31 - bit_offset)\n3. Call ProcessBitOperation on first word with calculated mask\n4. If operation returns 0, exit (typically indicates completion)\n5. Decrement word index\n6. Loop through remaining words from current to word 0 with mask=1\n7. Each iteration: call ProcessBitOperation, check result, decrement index\n8. Exit when all words processed or operation returns 0\n\nParameters:\n  pBitmapBase (dword *) - Base pointer to 32-bit word array containing bitmap\n  nBitOffset (int) - Starting bit offset into bitmap\n\nReturns:\n  void - Operation result indicated by side effects in buffer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If nBitOffset >= total bits in buffer, behavior depends on loop guard\n  - First word uses masked operation, subsequent words use mask=1\n  - Early exit when operation returns non-zero value\n  - Note: EDI register used as pBitmapWord pointer throughout function\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x20 (32) - Bits per word for division to get word index\n  0x1f (31) - Bit position for creating shift mask\n  1 - Mask value for complete word in loop\n\nStructure Layout:\nBitmap is an array of 32-bit words where each bit position represents a flag or state:\n  Offset | Size | Meaning\n  -------|------|--------\n  +0     |  4   | Word N (32 bits)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:a1fd1f83ab5d96b4bef4e8817dd3ae88",
