      "name": "GetDosErrnoPtr",
      "signature": "DWORD * GetDosErrnoPtr(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "DWORD *",
      "comment": "Returns a pointer to the error code field in the current thread's context structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetOrCreateThreadContext() to retrieve the thread context base pointer\n2. Calculate offset to error code field by adding 12 bytes (0xC) to base pointer\n3. Return the calculated pointer for direct error code access\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nDWORD * - Pointer to the error code field at offset +12 in ThreadContext structure\n          Used by callers to read/write thread-local error codes from GetLastError()\n\nStructure Layout:\nThreadContext structure (120 bytes total):\nOffset | Size | Field Name    | Type    | Description\n+0x00  | ?    | (unknown)     | ?       | Thread context base fields\n+0x0C  | 4    | dwErrorCode   | DWORD   | Last error code for this thread\n+0x10  | ?    | (remaining)   | ?       | Additional context fields\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xC (12) - Byte offset to dwErrorCode field in ThreadContext structure",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:b1691d6b7b8ba065c3fc1a089e8db64e",
