      "name": "GetCpuTimestampCounter",
      "signature": "ulonglong GetCpuTimestampCounter(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "ulonglong",
      "comment": "Retrieves the CPU timestamp counter (TSC) for high-resolution timing measurements.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Execute RDTSC instruction to atomically read the processor's timestamp counter register\n2. Processor returns 64-bit counter value split into EDX:EAX (EDX=high 32 bits, EAX=low 32 bits)\n3. Return the combined 64-bit value to caller\n\nParameters:\nNone - This function takes no parameters\n\nReturns:\nulonglong - 64-bit unsigned integer representing the processor's timestamp counter, increments at each clock cycle\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- RDTSC is typically synchronized across cores on modern processors but behavior varies by hardware\n- Counter wraps around after approximately 292 years on modern x86-64 systems (at 3+ GHz)\n- Execution cost is typically 24-40 clock cycles depending on processor model",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.08",
